review.summary:
The fix extends the existing automatic-result mechanism in `Acc` instead of adding a second one. `Acc.fail` now takes an optional rule and page. Deafened passes `GLOSS.deafened#2` and p.181 and carries the `SRD[...]` tag. When an effect supplies its own rule, `_finish` logs the automatic result under that rule and page; otherwise it keeps the caller's rule. Fail still overrides a success, and the first failure's reason, rule and page win, so the change is consistent. The rule lives in the effect layer, where the condition decides the result. Removing the T-94 xfail is right, because the acceptance test now passes.

The unit tests check behaviour:
- the logged check event cites the Deafened rule and page;
- a paralyzed save without a rule keeps the caller's rule;
- `Acc` keeps the first failure's rule;
- Deafened fails a hearing check but not a sight check.

All gates pass. I also ran the Deafened-filtered selection of the related test files: 17 passed. No scope creep beyond the `loop/costs.jsonl` bookkeeping line.
